  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "game-description-7a89b432-a8ed-4def-940e-1ddde74e765c-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Ice hockey is played on skates, with teams using sticks to move a puck and shoot it into a goal. Rapid transitions, passing lanes, and positional coordination shape play, while substitutions allow teams to sustain a high pace. Standard full-strength play puts five skaters and a goaltender on each side."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-7a89b432-a8ed-4def-940e-1ddde74e765c-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "The modern organized sport developed in Canada from several earlier traditions. An indoor game held in Montreal in 1875 is an important landmark in its recorded history, rather than proof of a single moment of invention. Competitive rules standardize rink markings, periods, penalties, and equipment."
    },
